{"name":"Kombu","hex":"#7e726d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kombu","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Edible kelp (“a type of brown seaweed”) (from the class Phaeophyceae) used in East Asian cuisine."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of long horn instrument from Tamil Nadu and Kerala."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kombu"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kombu","blocks":[{"text":"Kombu or Konbu is edible kelp mostly from the family Laminariaceae and is widely eaten in East Asia. It may also be referred to as dasima or haidai."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Kombu.jpg/330px-Kombu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kombu","wikidata":"Q11261547"},{"title":"Kombu (instrument)","blocks":[{"text":"The kombu or kompu, also known as kombu pattu, is a brass natural horn used primarily in the South Indian states of Tamil Nadu and Kerala. Usually played along with Panchavadyam, Pandi Melam, Panchari melam etc. This musical instrument is usually seen in south India. The instrument is like a long horn."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Kombu_%28instrument%29.jpg/330px-Kombu_%28instrument%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kombu_(instrument)","wikidata":"Q1779894"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Dried_kombu_in_a_supermarket.jpg/500px-Dried_kombu_in_a_supermarket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Dried_kombu_in_a_supermarket.jpg/1280px-Dried_kombu_in_a_supermarket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Dried_kombu_in_a_supermarket.jpg/500px-Dried_kombu_in_a_